*The candidate may draw or describe. A large labelled drawing with sharp continuous lines and a title is expected.*

**(i) A mould fungus (e.g. Mucor or Rhizopus, bread mould).** Draw a **mycelium**, a network of thread-like **hyphae** (no chlorophyll; the cell wall is made of **chitin**; the hyphae are multinucleate and not divided by cross walls). Label:
- **hyphae / mycelium** (growing on or in the food);
- **rhizoids** (anchor the fungus and absorb food; digestive enzymes are secreted onto the food);
- **stolon** (horizontal hypha joining groups of rhizoids, in Rhizopus);
- **sporangiophore** (upright hypha);
- **sporangium** (round, black when ripe, contains spores) with the **columella** at its base;
- **spores** (inside the sporangium).

**(ii) An Amoeba.** Draw an irregular, constantly changing microscopic cell (one cell, no fixed shape). Label:
- **cell (plasma) membrane** (thin, no cell wall);
- **cytoplasm**: clear outer **ectoplasm** and granular inner **endoplasm**;
- **nucleus** (one, controls the cell);
- **pseudopodia** (false feet, for movement and for engulfing food);
- **food vacuole** (digestion of engulfed food);
- **contractile vacuole** (removes excess water, osmoregulation).
